Yes, visibility hidden too. The device screen inherited. Best fix: rename the display element class to `device-display` and every `.screen` selector that targets display. But `.screen` is used in many phone CSS selectors and JS. Could simply add `#deviceScreen` overrides with enough specificity for all relevant properties:

#deviceScreen {
 position: absolute;
 inset: 3.4%;
 z-index: 8;
 display: flex;
 flex-direction: column;
 overflow: hidden;
 opacity: 1;
 visibility: visible;
 transform: none? but open state transform needs to work. Base sets transform translateY(14px) scale(.992) unless is-active. Need override transform: none for default, while `.phone.open #deviceScreen` etc. Could add higher specificity rules, but `.phone.open .screen` is specificity 0,2,1 vs #id 1,0,0; ID wins, so open transform wouldn't apply! Bad.

